# Desktop ↔ API match-data contract

## Hard rule

Never mark CS2 or Deadlock Analyse `ready` without rich Valve demo/replay stats (`hasRichMatchData`).

API `MatchDataQualityService::isReadyForCs2Desktop` rejects sparse jobs with `DEMO_NOT_READY` / `missing_coaching_inputs`.

## Before changing readiness

1. Keep desktop `getAnalysisReadiness` aligned with API readiness per game.
2. Update `electron/main/desktop-api-match-data-contract.test.ts`.
3. Run `npm test` (CI runs this on main / PRs).
4. Do not encode "VOD ready, attach demo later" as `ready: true`.
